abl_signed-SM8750.elf is the ROCKNIX ABL v1.1.8 payload for SM8750 (AYN Odin 3), unchanged.

Provenance (2026-09-27): ROCKNIX published v1.1.8 on 2026-08-25 at
  https://github.com/ROCKNIX/abl/releases/tag/v1.1.8
and removed the v1.1.5-v1.1.8 release assets on 2026-09-26 when v1.1.9 shipped (the URLs 404).
This copy is the byte-identical file ArmadaOS vendored into their tree the same day
(github.com/armada-os/armada, abl/, PR #560 merged 2026-09-27), whose sha256
  bedff34b99bd06202301e78ee5ee025b81d5144c9773de179b5f48ba3b38455a  (258048 bytes)
equals the 1.1.8 / SM8750 row of Armada's releases.tsv (computed from the original ROCKNIX
tarball) and of overlay/usr/share/holodor/rocknix-abl-releases.tsv here. The .sha256 sidecar
next to it is ours, in the release's format.

History: v1.1.7 (sha256 79e82279…) shipped on every Holodor image through 20260925. v1.1.8
ran on the development Odin 3 from 2026-09-15 (flashed by Armada's kit) through the 20260925
acceptance, booting Holodor from SD and internal, plus Android. Its menu has no device-model
step (auto "AYN Odin 3") and a strict boot-source setting (auto / Internal / SDCard).
v1.1.9 (2026-09-26, "bootcfw: simplify and speed up the boot process") is catalogued but not
adopted: untested here, and Armada is soaking it first.

The scripts in rocknix_abl/ are Holodor's versions of the ROCKNIX distribution's
packages/tools/rocknix-abl/sources (GPL-2.0). backup_abl.sh additionally copies
the backup to the SD card (verified on the device 2026-09-27), and
disable/enable_android_updates.sh are ours (disable_android_updates.sh does NOT work
from AYN's runner as of 2026-09-27: the update app stays usable; under investigation).
